# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The coordinator's working directory. NEVER committed.
#
# This holds real endpoint UUIDs, partner configs mid-negotiation, run outputs,
# and coordinator notes that quote partner correspondence. Sensitive material in
# git history is not really removable, so this rule exists from the first commit,
# before any content landed. See local/README.md and docs/coordinator/new-federation.md.
#
# The README is the one tracked file, so a collaborator who clones the repo can
# see why the directory exists and what belongs in it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
local/*
!local/README.md

# The real federation config: coordinator identity, live endpoint UUIDs, per-site
# assignments. The committed, fictional counterpart is federation.yaml.example.
federation.yaml
!federation.yaml.example

# Vendored non-Python binaries (SuSiEx, PLINK) installed by
# scripts/fine-mapping/install_*.sh. May be a real directory or a symlink into
# local/vendor/, so no trailing slash.
vendor

# Data. No experiment's inputs or outputs belong in git.
data/
outputs/
output/
*.bed
*.bim
*.fam
*.pgen
*.pvar
*.psam
*.vcf
*.vcf.gz
*.tar.gz
*.tgz

# Logs and run artifacts
*.log
.jobid

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.tox/
.nox/

# Test / coverage / type-check caches
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.hypothesis/

# Editors and OS
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store

# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Downloaded wheels. The offline installer drops these in the tree; they are
# install artifacts, not source, and constraints.txt already pins the versions.
*.whl

# Scheduler job output. The PBS scripts write here (`#PBS -o logs/...`), so the
# directory appears on any machine that has run one; none of it belongs in the repo.
logs/
